# Fleet inventory — which repositories get a self-hosted runner on this host.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/gh-runner/fleet (or point $GH_RUNNER_FLEET_FILE at it) and
# edit. One OWNER/REPO per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# It is not committed, and that is deliberate: this repository is public, and a
# list of which private repositories run on which machine is precisely the kind
# of inventory not to publish. The scripts read it from your config directory
# instead.
#
# Every repository listed here must be PRIVATE. mint-fleet-tokens.sh checks
# each one and refuses to mint a token for a public repository — a public
# repository accepts pull requests from anyone, its Actions minutes are free,
# and a self-hosted runner is a persistent machine that is not reset between
# jobs. See docs/RUNNER_FLEET.md.
#
# A runner serves exactly one repository, so each line below becomes one runner
# installation.

# owner/some-private-app
# owner/some-other-private-app
# another-owner/private-service
